WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
What about social changes?

2
00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:15.600
In my particular subject matter, it wasn’t terribly paramount because the commercial fishing industry and the trapping industry and the wetlands owners,

3
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:23.860
and anybody else you kind of deal with in my subject matter were overall heavily dominated by Caucasians.

4
00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:28.180
There was very little racial mix I ever had to deal with;

5
00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:38.020
until late in my career and that’s when Cambodian and Vietnamese fishermen came over after the war.

6
00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:52.240
And were being sponsored by Catholic charities and many other organizations and the atmosphere here in south Louisiana was very similar to coastal Vietnam and Cambodia, evidently.

7
00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:58.840
And they were artisanal fishermen and boat builders and people like that.

8
00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:08.240
And they came in and that was a big challenge for society in Louisiana.

9
00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:23.880
There were several incidents of boat rammings and sabotage and conflicts at sea and conflicts at the dock.

10
00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:29.000
But that went away pretty quickly, probably in five to ten years.

11
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:36.860
And the majority of the commercial shrimping fleet in the Gulf of Mexico now is Asian oriented.
